positive_text:
Let $\mathbb{R}^{5}$ be the space of all 5-tuples of real numbers $\left(a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}, a_{4}, a_{5}\right)$. Consider the set of all hyperplanes defined by:
- $a_{i}=a_{j}$ for all $1 \leq i<j \leq 5$;
- $a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+a_{4}+a_{5}=-1$;
- $a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+a_{4}+a_{5}=0$;
- $a_{1}+a_{2}+a_{3}+a_{4}+a_{5}=1$.
How many connected regions are created by these hyperplanes in $\mathbb{R}^{5}$?

negatives.text:
