Let $a$ be a real number. Show that there exists an affine function $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ such that $f(a) = 0$ if and only if $|a| \ge 4$, and $f$ satisfies the conditions:
(i) $|f(x)| \le 2$ for all $x$ with $|x| \le 2$;
(ii) $|f(x)| \ge 1$ for all $x$ with $|x| \le 1$.
